                               Linux File System

--> it is a way linux organize and store files and directories on a disk.

        Windows                                                     Linux
        C:\                                                           /

All configuration files are stored in                              
        C:\Windows                                                  /etc

home directory for users
       c:\user                                                      /home      

Installed software files
    C:\program files                                                /usr (Unix system Resource) 
                                                                       or 
                                                                    /opt
Temp files  
     C:\temp                                                        /tmp 

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/root : the root user directory
/boot : contains files required during the system boot process
POST : Power ON Self Test 
/dev : linux represents many devices as files under /dev
/mnt : temp location for mounting filesystem
/media : (removable media) commonly used for automatically mounted removable devics.
/var : (variable) logs and changing application data
/srv : (service) data for services




